Pump negative (−) connects to the external pump supply negative (−).

- Use COM and NO (normally open) so the pump is off when the relay is inactive.
- The pump must use a separate supply rated for its voltage and current.
- Verify that the relay contacts are rated for the pump's startup current. Keep water away from exposed electrical connections.
- Some relay modules are active-low, meaning a LOW signal turns the relay on. We'll account for that in the Arduino code and make the setting easy to change.
- Never connect the pump directly to an Arduino pin.
