1. Correct wiring for the two-leg moisture probe









Probe leg 1 → Arduino A0

This is the analog measurement point.












10 kΩ resistor → between Arduino 5V and A0

This acts as a pull-up and limits current through the probe.












Probe leg 2 → Arduino D12

The firmware briefly sets D12 LOW to take a reading, then returns it to input mode.



Wire it like this:
Arduino 5V
    |
  [10 kΩ]
    |
    +---------- Arduino A0
    |
  Probe leg 1
  [SOIL PROBE]
  Probe leg 2
    |
Arduino D12


Do not connect either probe leg directly to 5V or GND. The circuit above uses D12 as a switched measurement connection. Keep the probe away from the robot's water-pump wiring and wet electrical connections.
